@id n5_hugh
# DRAFT
# Prior Hugh at dusk, on the north walk (night 5, clear and cold). Grim; he means to see it ended tonight.
# (He arrests the porter at dawn. Nothing here says so.) He knows what happened in the chapter house. The blood on his
# sleeve (prior_sleeve): Wulfric's, and the porter was there first. Telling him what you've seen: Suspicion +10 (Ranulf overhears).
# Claims: n5_hugh_porter (mistaken): whatever is killing his brothers came in with the porter.
== start
(The prior is on the north walk, his tablet shut in his hand for once. He looks as if he hasn't slept.)
Hugh {cold}: Porter.
-> simon_dead [if died_simon]
-> simon_lived [if n5_saved=simon]
-> plain

== simon_dead
Hugh {cold}: A brother's throat cut on the chapter house floor, and the porter in the door. Thomas says you saved his life.
Hugh {cold, jaw}: Thomas is generous.
-> ended

== simon_lived
Hugh {grave}: Brother Simon says you pulled the man off him. He'll say nothing else. He shakes when I ask him.
-> ended

== plain
Hugh {cold, jaw}: Five nights since you came to that gate, and I've buried more brothers than in five years.
-> ended

== ended
Hugh {cold}: It ends tonight. One way or another, I'll have a name by Lauds.
-> topics

== again
(He's writing on his tablet again, and doesn't look up.)
Hugh {cold}: Go to your supper, porter.
-> topics

== topics
* [if prior_sleeve] [if not n5_hugh_sleeve] Whose blood is that on your sleeve, Father Prior? -> sleeve
* [if not n5_hugh_told] I'll tell you what I've seen, Father Prior. -> told
* [if not n5_hugh_means] What do you mean to do, Father Prior? -> means

== sleeve [set n5_hugh_sleeve]
(He looks down at the sleeve. It's been scrubbed. The stain is still there.)
Hugh {cold, jaw}: Wulfric's. I knelt by him in the fog. You saw me do it.
Hugh {cold}: You were there before me, porter. You're always there before me.
-> topics

# Telling the prior anything: Suspicion +10, because Ranulf overhears (design doc).
== told [set n5_hugh_told] [suspicion 10]
(You tell him. He opens the tablet and writes until the wax is full.)
(Across the garth, someone moves out of the light and is gone.)
Hugh {cold}: I've heard you. Whether I believe you is another matter. Go and keep your gate.
-> topics

== means [set n5_hugh_means]
Hugh {grave}: What a prior is for. Find who has been killing my brothers, and see him taken.
Hugh {cold}: Keep to your gate tonight, porter. Keep to it, and I'll know where to find you.
-> n5_hugh_porter

# He suspects the porter (design doc, cast table), and means it: his face is his honest one. But it isn't so: mistaken. Pressing him or showing him proof is the right read.
# Right is to show him better (docs/systems/mechanics.md, "The payoff": he believes the porter if shown enough).
== n5_hugh_porter [claim n5_hugh_porter mistaken]
Hugh {cold, jaw}: Every death in this house since you came to that gate, and the porter there before me. Whatever is killing my brothers, it came in with you.
* [believe] God help me, Father Prior. Perhaps it did. -> porter_believed
* [press] Then why am I not under lock, Father Prior? -> porter_pressed
* [confront osric_mask] The demon in the fog lost its mask, Father Prior. Under it was Brother Osric. -> porter_broken

== porter_believed
Hugh {cold}: Then pray on it, porter. You've until Lauds.
-> topics

== porter_pressed
Hugh {grave, look down}: (He's quiet a moment.) You'd be under lock, if I were sure of it. I'm not.
Hugh {cold, jaw}: One man didn't do all this, and I want every one of them. Go to your gate.
-> topics

# Telling the prior anything: Suspicion +10, because Ranulf overhears (design doc).
== porter_broken [suspicion 10]
(He looks at you a long moment. Then he opens the tablet and writes one word. Across the garth, a door shuts softly.)
Hugh {grave}: A face in the fog, from a porter who sees things in the smoke. It isn't enough.
Hugh {cold, jaw}: But I'll look at Osric. Bring me something I can hold in my hand, porter, and I'll look at more.
-> topics

== leave
Hugh {cold}: Lauds, porter. I'll know by Lauds.
